{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V15runConcurrentlyyySayAA16ConcurrentChangeVGF","role":"symbol","title":"runConcurrently(_:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"WorldModule","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Concurrency.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Concurrency.swift#L264"},"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changes","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ConcurrentChange","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"changes","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The changes to run."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this method to spread independent work across the processor’s cores. Each change reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the world as it was before any of them ran, and writes only the types its access lists, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result is the same as running the changes one after another in any order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Health(current: 10))","","world.runConcurrently([","    ConcurrentChange(access: .reads(Velocity.self).writes(Position.self)) { world in","        world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","        }","    },","    ConcurrentChange(access: .writes(Health.self)) { world in","        world.update(Health.self) { health, _ in health.current -= 1 }","    },","])","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball].x, world[Health.self, of: ball].current)","\/\/ Prints \"1.0 9\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change sees the components and resources that other changes write as missing, so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access must list everything it reads. Command buffers a change queues with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are queued in this world in the order of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change must write only the component and resource types its access lists,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and must not spawn or despawn entities. It writes relations through their "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, and the hierarchy through "},{"code":"Targets<ChildOf>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), besides the cost of the changes themselves, where "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"c"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number of changes and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of component types the world has stored."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No two accesses conflict, and each change writes only what its access"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lists and spawns and despawns nothing; a change that breaks this traps. In debug builds,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a change that reads a component or resource type its access doesn’t list traps too. Any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change may read "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrote.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/queue(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/queue(_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Adds a command buffer to the world’s queue, to apply later with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/applyQueuedCommands()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"queue(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"queue"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","text":"Commands"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/runConcurrently(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)","title":"runConcurrently(_:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrote."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries, updates, and commands."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule","title":"WorldModule","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Disabled":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Disabled"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Disabled","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Disabled"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/disabled","abstract":[{"text":"A component that makes queries and updates skip an entity, unless they ask for it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","title":"World","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","abstract":[{"text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources.","type":"text"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/ConcurrentChange":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcurrentChange"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A change to a world, paired with the access that describes what it reads and writes."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ConcurrentChange","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/concurrentchange","title":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcurrentChange"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/applyQueuedCommands()":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"applyQueuedCommands"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Entity","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/applyQueuedCommands()","title":"applyQueuedCommands()","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/applyqueuedcommands()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Applies every queued command buffer, in the order the buffers were queued, and empties the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queue."}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Targets":{"title":"Targets","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Targets","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/targets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The component that holds a source entity’s targets of a relation, with the relation’s value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for each."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Targets","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Prefab":{"title":"Prefab","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Prefab","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/prefab","abstract":[{"text":"A component that marks an entity as a template for spawning copies.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Prefab","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"}}}